  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fan Tan (Sevens). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
    objective: 'Corner the market by collecting all cards of one commodity before the other players do.',
    gameplay: 'Players simultaneously trade face-down sets of matching quantity, calling out how many cards they are offering. Trades are accepted by another player offering the same number. A player who completes a full commodity set calls the corner and scores the hand.',
    keyRules: [
      'Trades are simultaneous and must exchange equal numbers of cards.',
      'Players may not reveal the exact commodities being traded during the exchange.',
      'A complete commodity set wins the hand; editions with Bull and Bear cards add bonus and penalty cards.',
    ],
